  "rationale": "The workflow runs `npm install` on every push to main under `docs/**`, repeatedly fetching dependencies on each run. The P-LIT-GHA-CACHE pattern (Cache dependency downloads) supports caching dependency downloads; its preconditions are met because dependency fetching is repeated and the cache key can include the lockfile/environment inputs. Adding an `actions/cache@v4` step for `~/.npm` keyed on `package-lock.json`/`package.json` before `npm install` preserves every existing build and deploy step and required check, weakens no permissions, adds no secrets or privileged actions, and introduces no new network access beyond the standard GitHub Actions cache service.",
